abstract: >-
  DAIRM-TR-0001 (Technical Report / Working Draft, version 2.0.0) describes
  DAIRM, Divyendu's Data-State-Aware AI Reference Model, an informative
  reference model for the request path of generative AI inference serving.
  It defines a six-layer request path (L6 Application, L5 Orchestration &
  Gateway, L4 Serving Engine, L3 Model Execution Runtime, L2 Device & Driver,
  L1 Physical Compute & Interconnect) with Context Services, Build/Deploy and
  Management planes; a named, observable data state at every boundary
  (request payload, retrieved passages, enriched prompt, token-ID batch and
  KV-cache block table, kernel launch stream, device instruction and
  memory-transaction stream, token stream); a boundary-attributed latency
  diagnostic method; and a layer-indexed telemetry attribute set (dairm.*).
  DAIRM does not claim the layered-stack idea or the OSI analogy as novel and
  credits earlier OSI-inspired AI models. Version 2.0.0 supersedes AOSI v1.2.1:
  the model was renamed and restructured after the author's own (AI-assisted)
  review, not an external peer review, and an
  unsupported earlier drafting date was removed. Not an IETF RFC and not a
  standard.
